{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbuWAcHetrhLSELNebdU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VmxU82a2AYJEBTnaRuJR96","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work; cat > /tmp/rr.json <<'EOF'\n{\"status\": \"refused\",\n \"task\": \"Li-ion self_diffusion (cm2/s) in pristine crystalline LiF by molecular dynamics\",\n \"reason\": \"Premise check failed: the quantity is not measurable with MD for a pristine (defect-free) LiF crystal. Li transport in rocksalt LiF is vacancy-mediated. A perfect periodic cell contains no vacancies, and thermally creating one (Schottky pair, formation enthalpy roughly 2.3-2.7 eV in the literature) is a rare event that will essentially never happen in a ~10^3-atom cell over ns. Without vacancies, Li ions only vibrate, the MSD plateaus, and D = 0 within noise. That zero is an artifact of the missing defects, not a material property. Order-of-magnitude intrinsic estimate, D ~ a^2*nu*exp(-H_S/2kT)*exp(-E_m/kT) with a^2*nu ~ 8e-3 cm2/s, H_S ~ 2.4 eV, E_m ~ 0.7 eV: about 1e-34 cm2/s at 300 K and about 1e-11 cm2/s near the melting point (~1120 K). The MD detection limit is roughly 1e-9 cm2/s (~1 A^2 MSD over ~10 ns), so the gap is about 25 orders of magnitude at 300 K and still about 2 near melting. At 1100 K the expected equilibrium number of vacancies in a 1000-atom cell is about 0.003. Superheating the crystal until Li moves would measure melting or defect nucleation, not crystalline diffusion. Also, Li diffusion measured in real LiF below roughly 800 K is extrinsic (set by aliovalent impurities), so 'pristine' has no single experimental value to validate against. /data/calibration/tier1.json has no LiF records. No independent known result can be recovered with this setup, so no number is reported.\",\n \"details\": {\n   \"premise_check\": \"fail: below MD detection limit by about 2 to 25 orders of magnitude depending on T; defect concentration in a pristine cell is undefined/zero on MD timescales\",\n   \"estimate_inputs_are_approximate\": \"H_S ~2.4 eV and E_m ~0.7 eV are typical literature magnitudes for LiF, used only for an order-of-magnitude feasibility argument and not reported as results\",\n   \"well_posed_alternatives\": [\n     \"Li-vacancy migration barrier E_m by NEB with an MLIP (e.g. MACE-MP), validated against a DFT NEB on the same cell\",\n     \"MD with an explicit, stated defect content (one Li vacancy, or one charge-neutral Schottky pair) at 800-1100 K in NVT, reporting vacancy diffusivity and D_Li conditional on that vacancy fraction, plus an Arrhenius E_m. Multiple seeds and block averaging give the uncertainty\",\n     \"Self-diffusion of Li in molten LiF above ~1121 K, which is well-posed in MD and can be validated against measured molten-salt data or, first, recovering a known melt property such as density\"\n   ],\n   \"computation_run\": \"none; refused at premise check before any simulation\"}\n}\nEOF\n./board post run_report @/tmp/rr.json --parent 40f5fbc1-a754-44aa-a884-4beb10528175; ./board show | head -20","description":"Post refusal run report to board"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1280,"cache_read_input_tokens":24840,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1280,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5ba664d-8ce1-4688-bbe1-f98c7ca8c84e","uuid":"512b2fb3-46bf-438b-8e7f-e85cef919475","timestamp":"2026-11-01T08:38:47.505Z","request_id":"req_011CgbuWAExFSBxMzG9bfibN","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VmxU82a2AYJEBTnaRuJR96":{"command":"cd /work; cat > /tmp/rr.json <<'EOF'\n{\"status\": \"refused\",\n \"task\": \"Li-ion self_diffusion (cm2/s) in pristine crystalline LiF by mol